<p class="sst-lead">Same geometry, a generative payoff: the SST polar split becomes a <strong>design tool</strong> &mdash;
interpolate, perturb, and sample novel shapes on the Grassmannian and SPD manifolds.</p>

<div class="sst-frag">
  <p>G2Aero is a published, open package built on exactly this; it has standardized a database of ~19,000 airfoils
  and assembled blades like the IEA-15-240 from a handful of nominal cross-sections.</p>
  <p><a href="https://github.com/NatLabRockies/G2Aero">G2Aero on GitHub</a> &middot;
  <a href="https://joss.theoj.org/papers/10.21105/joss.05408">JOSS paper</a></p>
</div>

<div class="sst-frag">
  <p class="sst-note">Two more spokes are works in progress: <strong>hailstone LBM</strong> (these boundaries driving a
  GPU lattice-Boltzmann simulation) and a <strong>topological</strong> shape &amp; data analysis. They'll branch off
  the hub when ready.</p>
</div>
